  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Atlantic Diving Supply reported $3.3B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date across 52,193 awards, with an average award size of $64.1K. Obligations fell 44.2% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $3.2B this fiscal year to date. Other federal buyers include the General Services Administration at $93.5M and the Department of Homeland Security at $31.3M. Sales cluster in a few NAICS markets. Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers is the largest market at $1.9B, followed by All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing at $982M and Bare Printed Circuit Board Manufacturing at $105M. Historical obligations show growth through FY25, peaking at $6B, then moving to $3.3B in FY26 to date. The combination of many small awards and a small number of large agency relationships shapes the vendor profile. Contractors and agency buyers searching for pricing, lead times, or subcontracting partners should note the concentration with the Department of Defense and the prominence of merchant wholesaler and miscellaneous manufacturing markets.",
    "sections": [
